# Modelfile: Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, 32K context — "32k-standalone" tuning for
# graceful context-limit handling (Legion 5 Pro, 8GB VRAM/32GB RAM, no swap).
#
# Named "standalone" because Copilot CLI's static system+tool overhead alone
# (~21.5K tokens, see the 64k-agentic Modelfile) doesn't fit this window —
# use this variant with `ollama run qwen3.6:35b-a3b-32k-standalone` directly,
# not through Copilot CLI / opencode.
#
# Goal: never silently stop mid-thinking with no visible reply. See
# docs/tuning-results.md ("Output-side testing" + "no-swap host") for the
# evidence behind these choices:
#   - num_ctx 32768 chosen as the daily-driver default for plain chat: lowest/
#     most predictable RAM pressure of all tested sizes, most headroom now
#     that there's no swap cushion. Use 64k-agentic for CLI/tool-calling use,
#     or any task needing more room (large doc/RAG input).
#   - num_predict capped at 16384 (50% of num_ctx) — not -1/unbounded, and
#     raised from an earlier 8192 after repeated real-world "terminated
#     mid-think / truncated output" incidents. Guarantees generation always
#     stops on its own terms with tokens already returned, instead of
#     silently riding the model's "thinking" phase all the way to num_ctx,
#     while giving thinking+response a much larger runway than before. The
#     conversation-history side of the window is intentionally left smaller
#     (only 16384 tokens of "room" before context-shift kicks in) because
#     that side already degrades gracefully on its own (oldest-turn
#     eviction, confirmed via context-probe tests) — it doesn't need a big
#     reserved cushion the way single-turn output does.
#   - SYSTEM prompt nudges concise thinking so the cap above is rarely hit
#     in the first place, and pushes the model to commit to a final answer
#     rather than keep deliberating.
#   - Multi-turn conversations already degrade gracefully on their own:
#     Ollama's context-shift silently evicts oldest turns as num_ctx fills
#     (confirmed via context-probe tests) — no config needed for that case.
#     This tuning targets the *other* failure mode: long single-shot
#     generations/thinking that can hit num_ctx before finishing.

FROM qwen3.6:35b-a3b

PARAMETER num_ctx 32768
# num_gpu intentionally omitted — host-wide OLLAMA_NUM_GPU/OLLAMA_MAX_VRAM
# env vars already handle GPU offload; a static value here conflicts with it.
PARAMETER num_batch 256
PARAMETER num_thread 16

# Sampling aligned to Qwen3.6/Unsloth's published "thinking mode, precise
# coding" recommendation (temp 0.6 / top_p 0.95 / presence_penalty 0.0),
# same rationale as qwen3.6__35b-a3b-64k-agentic/Modelfile — see there and
# docs/tuning-results.md ("Unsloth alignment") for the full comparison.
PARAMETER temperature 0.6
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER presence_penalty 0.0

# 50/50 split of the 32K window: up to 16K for thinking+response in a single
# turn, 16K left for accumulated conversation/tool-context (relies on
# context-shift to evict oldest turns gracefully once that fills).
PARAMETER num_predict 16384

SYSTEM """You are a helpful assistant. Keep your internal reasoning
efficient and proportional to the difficulty of the question — do not
over-deliberate on simple requests. Regardless of how much you have
reasoned, always make sure to produce a clear, complete final answer
before you finish; if you notice you are running low on room to respond,
wrap up your reasoning early and give your best answer rather than leaving
it incomplete.
"""
